  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> be the of all column matrices <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math> and the system of equations (in real variables)<br /><math><mtable><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable></math><br />has at least one solution. Then, which of the following system(s) (in real variables) has (have) at least one solution of each <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#1013;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>S</mi></math> ?",
    "image": null
  },
